course: dictionary
lesson: 13299
title: Formal words: gratuity
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are formal. You will see them on bills, signs and letters, and grown-ups use them when they want to sound polite and careful. Gratuity is one of these words. Look at the clues around it to find its meaning.
explain: «The bill was £40, with a 10% gratuity added.» The bill is about money, and added means extra money on top of the price. So a gratuity must be extra money. Check by swapping in tip: «with a 10% tip added» still makes sense, so tip is a good meaning.
explain: «Gratuity included» on a menu tells you the extra money for good service is already in the price. «No gratuities» means you do not need to add any extra money. Look for clue words such as bill, included and added.
fact: Gratuity means a tip: extra money you give to say thank you for good service.
fact: A gratuity can also be a sum of money given to a worker when they leave a job.
fact: «Gratuity included» on a bill means the tip is already added to the price.
fact: «A 10% gratuity» means 10 pounds for every 100 pounds, so a £40 bill with a 10% gratuity adds £4.
fact: Gratuity is a formal word; the everyday word for it is tip.
exercise: «The waiter was very kind, so we left a gratuity on the table.» What is a gratuity here? | A bill for the food | *A thank-you tip | A rude remark | A type of table
exercise: The menu said «gratuity included». What does this tell you? | You must pay nothing at all | *The tip is already added to the bill | You must cook your own meal | The food is free
exercise: «Ravi received a gratuity when he left his job after ten years.» What is a gratuity? | A new job | A type of uniform | A holiday | *Money given to a worker when they leave
test: «The bill was £50, and a 10% gratuity was added.» How much is 10% of £50? | £10 | £50 | £15 | *£5
test: Which everyday word means nearly the same as gratuity? | *Tip | Bill | Table | Menu
exam: «No gratuities» on a sign means what? | You must add extra money for good service | *You do not need to add any extra money | The food is free | You must sing for your meal
